ding","depth":4,"id":"gemini-native-models-nanobanana","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini Native Models (NanoBanana)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini native image models use a template literal size format: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"aspectRatio_resolution\""},{"type":"text","value":". Each model accepts its own set, narrowed at compile time:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aspect Ratios"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolutions"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3.1-flash-image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1:1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2:3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3:2"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3:4"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4:3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4:5"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"5:4"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9:16"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"16:9"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"21:9"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1:4"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4:1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1:8"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"8:1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"512"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1K"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2K"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4K"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"same 14 as above (see note)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1K"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-nano-banana-2.1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"same 14 as above"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1K"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2K"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4K"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3-pro-image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1:1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2:3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3:2"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3:4"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4:3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4:5"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"5:4"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9:16"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"16:9"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"21:9"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1K"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2K"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4K"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-2.5-flash-image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"same 10 as above"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none — bare ratio"}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"// Examples\nsize: \"16:9_4K\"; // Widescreen at 4K resolution\nsize: \"1:1_2K\"; // Square at 2K resolution\nsize: \"1:8_512\"; // Tall banner at the 512 (0.5K) tier — Flash Image only\nsize: \"16:9\"; // gemini-2.5-flash-image: bare ratio, no resolution suffix","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"K"},{"type":"text","value":" is case-sensitive ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1k"},{"type":"text","value":" is rejected by the API), the smallest tier's token is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"512"},{"type":"text","value":" (not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"512px"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.5K"},{"type":"text","value":"), and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9:21"},{"type":"text","value":" is Vertex/Cloud-only so it is not accepted. Google documents no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image_size"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-2.5-flash-image"},{"type":"text","value":", so that model takes a bare aspect ratio and the adapter sends no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"imageSize"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The four extreme banner ratios ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1:4"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4:1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1:8"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"8:1"},{"type":"text","value":") are partially inferred for this model. Unlike the other three, Flash Lite has no per-model ratio table in Google's Gemini API guide; the 14-value set comes from the Cloud model page's explicit enumeration plus the guide's bare \"a discrete set of 14 aspect ratios\" assertion. The only Gemini-API enumeration for it is a 10-item bullet headed \"New aspect ratios\", which we read as a what's-new list rather than an exhaustive one. If the API rejects those four in practice, prefer the 10 standard ratios on this model."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"gemini-imagen-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini Imagen Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Imagen models accept WIDTHxHEIGHT format, which maps to aspect ratios internally:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Size"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aspect Ratio"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1024x1024"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1:1"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1920x1080"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"16:9"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1080x1920"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9:16"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, you can specify the aspect ratio directly in Model Options:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"imagen-4.0-generate-001\"),\n  prompt: \"A landscape photo\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    aspectRatio: \"16:9\",\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"image-conditioned-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image-Conditioned Generation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For image-to-image, reference-guided, multi-reference, and edit / inpaint\nflows, pass the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" as an ordered array of content parts — the same\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextPart"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImagePart"},{"type":"text","value":" shapes used elsewhere for multimodal content:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Turn this into a cinematic product photo\" },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/product.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Part order is meaningful. Providers with natively multimodal prompts\n(Gemini image models, OpenRouter) receive the parts exactly as written, so\ntext can refer to its neighbouring images:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\nimport { badExampleUrl, goodExampleUrl } from \"./urls\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Not like this\" },\n    { type: \"image\", source: { type: \"url\", value: badExampleUrl } },\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"more like this\" },\n    { type: \"image\", source: { type: \"url\", value: goodExampleUrl } },\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers with named request fields (OpenAI, fal, xAI) extract the image\nparts and flatten the text (text parts are joined verbatim, paragraph\nseparated)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The accepted part types are narrowed "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per model at compile time"}]},{"type":"text","value":": passing\nan image part to a text-only model (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dall-e-3"},{"type":"text","value":", Imagen) is a type\nerror, not just a runtime throw."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"referencing-images-from-your-prompt","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Referencing images from your prompt"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your prompt text is always sent verbatim — the SDK never injects or\nrewrites referencing markers."}]},{"type":"text","value":" When you want the text to refer to specific\ninput images, write the provider's own convention yourself:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convention"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (gpt-image)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Indexed prose, per OpenAI's prompting guide"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"apply the style of image 2 to image 1\""}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FLUX.2 on fal / BFL"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Indexed prose (BFL's docs parse "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image N"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"subject from image 1, style from image 2\""}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (native image models)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Describe the reference by content/role"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"using the attached fabric sample as the texture\""}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal Kling / Seedance endpoints"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@"},{"type":"text","value":"-tags, 1-indexed by input order"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"Put @Image1 in the style of @Image2\""}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"xAI grok-imagine"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No in-prompt syntax — images addressed in request order"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"render the product in the style of the second image\""}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To keep track of which part you meant by \"image 2\" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@Image2"},{"type":"text","value":", you can\nlabel parts with the informational "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tag"},{"type":"text","value":" field — the SDK ignores\nit, but it keeps your code self-documenting:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"prompt: [\n  { type: \"text\", content: \"Put @Image1 in the style of @Image2\" },\n  {\n    type: \"image\",\n    source: { type: \"url\", value: productUrl },\n    metadata: { tag: \"product\" },\n  },\n  {\n    type: \"image\",\n    source: { type: \"url\", value: styleUrl },\n    metadata: { tag: \"style\" },\n  },\n];","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"source-format","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source format"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImagePart.source"},{"type":"text","value":" is a discriminated union supporting both URLs and inline\nbase64 data — pass whichever you have:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// URL source\n{ type: 'image', source: { type: 'url', value: 'https://example.com/img.png' } }\n\n// Inline base64 data (mimeType required)\n{ type: 'image', source: { type: 'data', value: base64String, mimeType: 'image/png' } }","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini native image generation does not download a URL in your runtime. The adapter sends the URL as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"uri"},{"type":"text","value":". Gemini reads that URL. These sources work:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A public HTTPS URL"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files API"}]},{"type":"text","value":" URI"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gs://"},{"type":"text","value":" reference"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two paths have no URL passthrough and must upload real bytes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/images/edits"},{"type":"text","value":", and Sora "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input_reference"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Veo"}]},{"type":"text","value":": its predict API accepts only inline bytes or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gs://"},{"type":"text","value":"\nreference."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For these, an HTTP(S) URL input would have to be downloaded and buffered in\nmemory, which can OOM memory-constrained runtimes (e.g. Cloudflare Workers). So\nby default they "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"throw"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on an HTTP(S) URL image input rather than fetch it.\nPass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data:"},{"type":"text","value":" URI (or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gs://"},{"type":"text","value":" reference for Veo), or opt into fetching with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowUrlFetch"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createOpenaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\n// Opt into downloading + buffering HTTP(S) URL image inputs (server runtimes\n// with headroom). data: URIs always work without this flag.\nconst adapter = createOpenaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\", apiKey, {\n  allowUrlFetch: true,\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowUrlFetch"},{"type":"text","value":" option exists on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiVideo"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGeminiVideo"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"role-hints-via-metadata-role","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Role hints via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.role"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a generation has multiple inputs with different roles (mask vs reference\nvs start/end frame), set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.role"},{"type":"text","value":" on each part. Adapters route by role\nto the provider-specific field; parts without a role fall back to positional\nmapping."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Role"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maps to"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'reference'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reference_image_urls"},{"type":"text","value":"; Gemini multimodal part; positional fallback"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'character'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'reference'"},{"type":"text","value":"; Veo "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"referenceImages"},{"type":"text","value":" slot (planned — no Veo adapter yet)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'mask'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mask"},{"type":"text","value":" (gpt-image-2, gpt-image-1, dall-e-2); fal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mask_url"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'control'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"control_image_url"},{"type":"text","value":" (ControlNet / depth / pose conditioning)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'start_frame'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start_image_url"},{"type":"text","value":"; Veo "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image"},{"type":"text","value":" (planned) (used by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVideo"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'end_frame'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end_image_url"},{"type":"text","value":"; Veo "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastFrame"},{"type":"text","value":" (planned) (used by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVideo"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"inpaint-edit-with-a-mask","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inpaint / edit with a mask"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { photoUrl, maskUrl } from \"./urls\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Replace the masked region with a tree\" },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: photoUrl },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: maskUrl },\n      metadata: { role: \"mask\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"multi-reference-composition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multi-reference composition"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content:\n        \"Generate a new image of the product using the style of the second reference\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/product.png\" },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/style.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"provider-support","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider support"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-2.5-flare"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-2.5-sunburst"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-2"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-1"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-1-mini"},{"type":"text","value":" → routes to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"images.edit()"},{"type":"text","value":", up to 16 source images plus optional mask."},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<br>"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dall-e-2"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"images.edit()"},{"type":"text","value":" with 1 source image only."},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<br>"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dall-e-3"},{"type":"text","value":" → throws (no edit support)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native models send each prompt part as an Interactions content block, in the same order. Up to 14 input images. The SDK does not enforce that limit."},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<br>"},{"type":"text","value":"To edit the last image, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result.id"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.previous_interaction_id"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not send that image again. A new image part on that call is an extra reference. See "},{"type":"link","href":"#edit-a-gemini-native-image","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Edit a Gemini native image"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<br>"},{"type":"text","value":"Imagen throws on an image part. Imagen does not chain."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal.ai"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field names resolve per endpoint from a map generated from the fal SDK's endpoint types (e.g. nano-banana edit gets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image_urls"},{"type":"text","value":", Fooocus masks get "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mask_image_url"},{"type":"text","value":"). Defaults for unknown endpoints: 1 input → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image_url"},{"type":"text","value":"; multiple → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image_urls"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: 'mask'"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mask_url"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: 'control'"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"control_image_url"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: 'reference'"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'character'"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reference_image_urls"},{"type":"text","value":". Override with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" for endpoint-specific fields."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"grok-imagine models → xAI's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/images/edits"},{"type":"text","value":" (up to 3 source images, addressed by xAI in request order; prompt sent verbatim). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: 'mask'"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'control'"},{"type":"text","value":" throw (no Imagine API equivalent)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prompt parts map 1:1 onto multimodal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image_url"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" content parts, preserving interleaved order, and are forwarded to the underlying image model. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.strength"},{"type":"text","value":" (0.0–1.0) controls image-to-image influence on models that document it (e.g. Recraft). One image per request — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"numberOfImages > 1"},{"type":"text","value":" throws (the gateway ignores count keys)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BytePlus"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Seedream models → every input image is a plain reference on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image"},{"type":"text","value":" field (up to 14, or 10 on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dola-seedream-5-0-pro-260628"},{"type":"text","value":"). There is no mask, control or frame channel, so any role other than "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'reference'"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'character'"},{"type":"text","value":" throws rather than being silently flattened."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"n/a — no image generation API."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters that don't support image-conditioned generation throw a clear\nruntime error so calls fail fast rather than silently dropping the inputs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"full-stack-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full-Stack Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a React + Start walkthrough with OpenRouter, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/generate-image","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate Image"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI provides React hooks and server-side streaming helpers to build full-stack image generation with minimal boilerplate."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" To keep a batch across reloads, or to keep the images after the\nprovider's URLs expire, add "},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/generation-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation Persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"streaming-mode-server-route-client-hook","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming Mode (Server Route + Client Hook)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Create an API route that wraps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage"},{"type":"text","value":" as a streaming response:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/generate/image.ts\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { createFileRoute } from \"@tanstack/react-router\";\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute(\"/api/generate/image\")({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body = await request.json();\n        const { prompt, size, model, numberOfImages } = body.data;\n\n        const stream = generateImage({\n          adapter: openaiImage(model ?? \"dall-e-3\"),\n          prompt,\n          size,\n          numberOfImages,\n          stream: true,\n        });\n\n        return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n      },\n    },\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateImage"},{"type":"text","value":" hook with a connection adapter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateImage, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, reset } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/generate/image\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: \"A sunset over mountains\" })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? \"Generating...\" : \"Generate\"}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img\n          key={i}\n          src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`}\n          alt={img.revisedPrompt || \"Generated image\"}\n        />\n      ))}\n      {result && <button onClick={reset}>Clear</button>}\n    </div>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The other two transports (a server function returning JSON, or one returning an\nSSE "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":") work the same way here. They are in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#other-transports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced: other transports"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and explained once in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./generations#transports-in-full","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generations"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hook-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateImage"},{"type":"text","value":" hook accepts:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ConnectionAdapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming transport (SSE, HTTP stream, custom)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetcher"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(input) => Promise<ImageGenerationResult | Response>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct async function, or server function returning an SSE "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable scope for this generation. Required when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" is on. Optional for ephemeral runs."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Additional body parameters (connection mode)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(result) => TOutput | null | void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callback when images are generated. Optionally return a transformed value to store as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(error) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callback on error"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onProgress"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(progress, message?) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Progress updates (0-100)"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And returns:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(input: ImageGenerateInput) => Promise<void>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trigger generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImageGenerationResult | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The result, or null"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether generation is in progress"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current error, if any"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationClientState"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'idle'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'generating'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'success'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'error'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Abort the current generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear result, error, and return to idle"}]}]]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tip:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" To trigger image generation from your React, Vue, or Svelte app with loading states and error handling, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./generation-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation Hooks"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"advanced","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reference detail you do not need to get this working."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"other-transports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other transports"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"direct-mode-server-function-fetcher","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct Mode (Server Function + Fetcher)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For non-streaming usage with TanStack Start server functions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from \"@tanstack/react-start\";\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport const generateImageFn = createServerFn({ method: \"POST\" })\n  .inputValidator((data: { prompt: string; model?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    return generateImage({\n      adapter: openaiImage(data.model ?? \"dall-e-3\"),\n      prompt: data.prompt,\n    });\n  });","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"// components/ImageGenerator.tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { generateImageFn } from \"../lib/server-functions\";\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateImage({\n    fetcher: (data) => generateImageFn({ data }),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: \"A sunset over mountains\" })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img key={i} src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`} />\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"server-function-streaming-fetcher-response","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Function Streaming (Fetcher + Response)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For TanStack Start server functions that stream results. The fetcher receives type-safe input and returns an SSE "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":" — the client parses it automatically:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from \"@tanstack/react-start\";\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport const generateImageStreamFn = createServerFn({ method: \"POST\" })\n  .inputValidator((data: { prompt: string; model?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(({ data }) => {\n    return toServerSentEventsResponse(\n      generateImage({\n        adapter: openaiImage(data.model ?? \"dall-e-3\"),\n        prompt: data.prompt,\n        stream: true,\n      }),\n    );\n  });","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { generateImageStreamFn } from \"../lib/server-functions\";\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateImage({\n    fetcher: (input) => generateImageStreamFn({ data: input }),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: \"A sunset over mountains\" })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img key={i} src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`} />\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"openai-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Model Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI models support model-specific Model Options:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"gpt-image-2-gpt-image-1-gpt-image-1-mini","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GPT-Image-2 / GPT-Image-1 / GPT-Image-1-Mini"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"A cat wearing a hat\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    quality: \"high\", // 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' | 'auto'\n    background: \"transparent\", // 'transparent' | 'opaque' | 'auto'\n    output_format: \"png\", // 'png' | 'jpeg' | 'webp'\n    moderation: \"low\", // 'low' | 'auto'\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-2.5-flare"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-2.5-sunburst"},{"type":"text","value":" also take "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"quality: \"xhigh\""},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"quality: \"max\""},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"dall-e-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DALL-E 3"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"dall-e-3\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic car\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    quality: \"hd\", // 'hd' | 'standard'\n    style: \"vivid\", // 'vivid' | 'natural'\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"gemini-imagen-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini Imagen Model Options"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"imagen-4.0-generate-001\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful garden\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    aspectRatio: \"16:9\",\n    // personGeneration accepts PersonGeneration enum values: 'DONT_ALLOW' | 'ALLOW_ADULT' | 'ALLOW_ALL'\n    personGeneration: \"ALLOW_ADULT\",\n    negativePrompt: \"blurry, low quality\",\n    addWatermark: true,\n    outputMimeType: \"image/png\", // 'image/png' | 'image/jpeg' | 'image/webp'\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"gemini-native-model-options-nanobanana","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini Native Model Options (NanoBanana)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set native image options on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage, ThinkingLevel } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful garden\",\n  size: \"16:9_4K\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    seed: 42,\n    thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.LOW },\n    systemInstruction: \"Always render in watercolor.\",\n    // imageConfig replaces one field from size. The 16:9 ratio from size stays.\n    // imageConfig accepts only aspectRatio and imageSize.\n    imageConfig: { imageSize: \"2K\" },\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel"},{"type":"text","value":" to one of these values:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingLevel.LOW"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingLevel.MEDIUM"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingLevel.HIGH"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"thinkingConfig.thinkingBudget"},{"type":"text","value":" throws."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemInstruction"},{"type":"text","value":" contains an image, a file, or a tool call, the call throws."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the last result "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previous_interaction_id"},{"type":"text","value":". Read "},{"type":"link","href":"#edit-a-gemini-native-image","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Edit a Gemini native image"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the edit steps."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"safetySettings"},{"type":"text","value":" takes the SDK's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HarmCategory"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HarmBlockThreshold"},{"type":"text","value":" enums, so plain strings won't type-check. Both are re-exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-gemini"},{"type":"text","value":" — you don't need "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@google/genai"},{"type":"text","value":" in your own dependencies:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport {\n  HarmBlockThreshold,\n  HarmCategory,\n  geminiImage,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful garden\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    safetySettings: [\n      {\n        category: HarmCategory.HARM_CATEGORY_HATE_SPEECH,\n        threshold: HarmBlockThreshold.BLOCK_ONLY_HIGH,\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter always requests an image."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"response-format","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Response Format"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The image generation result includes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { TokenUsage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\ninterface ImageGenerationResult {\n  id: string; // Unique identifier for this generation\n  model: string; // The model used\n  images: GeneratedImage[]; // Array of generated images\n  // Canonical TokenUsage (same shape as chat). Token-billed models also surface\n  // a per-modality breakdown on `promptTokensDetails` (e.g. text vs image input\n  // tokens for gpt-image-1). Usage-billed providers (fal) instead surface\n  // `usage.billed` ({ quantity, unit }) — see the note below.\n  usage?: TokenUsage;\n}\n\ninterface GeneratedImage {\n  b64Json?: string; // Base64 encoded image data\n  url?: string; // URL to the image (OpenAI only)\n  revisedPrompt?: string; // Revised prompt (OpenAI only)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On a Gemini native image model, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" is the interaction id. Pass that id as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previous_interaction_id"},{"type":"text","value":" on the next edit."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cost tracking (fal):"}]},{"type":"text","value":" fal bills by usage-based units rather than tokens. The\nfal image adapter surfaces the real billed quantity as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage.billed"},{"type":"text","value":" —\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ quantity, unit: 'units' }"},{"type":"text","value":", read from fal's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-fal-billable-units"},{"type":"text","value":" result\nheader. Multiply the quantity by the endpoint's unit price from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET https://api.fal.ai/v1/models/pricing?endpoint_id=…"},{"type":"text","value":" for the exact cost —\nno "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":" interceptor needed."}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { falImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-fal\";\nimport { unitPrice } from \"./pricing\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: falImage(\"fal-ai/flux/dev\"),\n  prompt: \"a serene mountain lake\",\n});\n\nif (result.usage?.billed) {\n  const { quantity, unit } = result.usage.billed;\n  const cost = quantity * unitPrice; // unitPrice from fal pricing API\n  console.log(`Billed ${quantity} ${unit} (~$${cost})`);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"model-availability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model Availability"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"openai-models-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Models"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Images per Request"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-2.5-flare"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1-10"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-2.5-sunburst"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1-10"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1-10"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1-10"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-image-1-mini"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1-10"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dall-e-3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dall-e-2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1-10"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"gemini-native-models-nanobanana-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini Native Models (NanoBanana)"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3.1-flash-image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nano Banana 2 — latest and fastest Gemini native image generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nano Banana 2 Lite — ultra-low-latency, low-cost image generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-nano-banana-2.1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nano Banana 2.1 (1K/2K/4K, no 512 tier)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3-pro-image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nano Banana Pro — higher quality Gemini native image generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-2.5-flash-image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nano Banana — legacy; shuts down 2026-10-02"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3-pro-image-preview"},{"type":"text","value":" ids were shut down on 2026-06-25. They remain in the type union as deprecated aliases so existing code compiles, but calls to them fail — use the GA ids above."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"gemini-imagen-models-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini Imagen Models"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Images per Request"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"imagen-4.0-ultra-generate-001"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1-4"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"imagen-4.0-generate-001"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1-4"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"imagen-4.0-fast-generate-001"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1-4"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"error-handling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image generation can fail for various reasons. The adapters validate inputs before making API calls:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\ntry {\n  const result = await generateImage({\n    adapter: openaiImage(\"dall-e-3\"),\n    prompt: \"A cat\",\n    size: \"512x512\", // Invalid size for DALL-E 3 — throws at runtime\n  });\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.error(error.message);\n    // \"Size \"512x512\" is not supported by model \"dall-e-3\".\n    //  Supported sizes: 1024x1024, 1792x1024, 1024x1792\"\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The image adapters use the same environment variables as the text adapters:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (including NanoBanana): "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GEMINI_API_KEY"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BytePlus"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (Seedream): "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ARK_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BYTEPLUS_API_KEY"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"explicit-api-keys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit API Keys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For production use or when you need explicit control:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createOpenaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { createGeminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\n// OpenAI\nconst openaiAdapter = createOpenaiImage(\"dall-e-3\", \"your-openai-api-key\");\n\n// Gemini\nconst geminiAdapter = createGeminiImage(\n  \"imagen-4.0-generate-001\",\n  \"your-google-api-key\",\n);","lang":"typescript"}],"headings":[{"id":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"openai-image-generation","text":"OpenAI Image Generation","level":3},{"id":"gemini-image-generation","text":"Gemini Image Generation","level":3},{"id":"edit-a-gemini-native-image","text":"Edit a Gemini native image","level":4},{"id":"byteplus-image-generation","text":"BytePlus Image Generation","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"common-options","text":"Common Options","level":3},{"id":"size-options","text":"Size Options","level":3},{"id":"openai-models","text":"OpenAI Models","level":4},{"id":"gemini-native-models-nanobanana","text":"Gemini Native Models (NanoBanana)","level":4},{"id":"gemini-imagen-models","text":"Gemini Imagen Models","level":4},{"id":"image-conditioned-generation","text":"Image-Conditioned Generation","level":2},{"id":"referencing-images-from-your-prompt","text":"Referencing images from your prompt","level":3},{"id":"source-format","text":"Source format","level":3},{"id":"role-hints-via-metadata-role","text":"Role hints via metadata.role","level":3},{"id":"inpaint-edit-with-a-mask","text":"Inpaint / edit with a mask","level":4},{"id":"multi-reference-composition","text":"Multi-reference composition","level":4},{"id":"provider-support","text":"Provider support","level":3},{"id":"full-stack-usage","text":"Full-Stack Usage","level":2},{"id":"streaming-mode-server-route-client-hook","text":"Streaming Mode (Server Route + Client Hook)","level":3},{"id":"hook-api","text":"Hook API","level":3},{"id":"advanced","text":"Advanced","level":2},{"id":"other-transports","text":"Other transports","level":3},{"id":"direct-mode-server-function-fetcher","text":"Direct Mode (Server Function + Fetcher)","level":4},{"id":"server-function-streaming-fetcher-response","text":"Server Function Streaming (Fetcher + Response)","level":4},{"id":"model-options","text":"Model Options","level":3},{"id":"openai-model-options","text":"OpenAI Model Options","level":4},{"id":"gpt-image-2-gpt-image-1-gpt-image-1-mini","text":"GPT-Image-2 / GPT-Image-1 / GPT-Image-1-Mini","level":5},{"id":"dall-e-3","text":"DALL-E 3","level":5},{"id":"gemini-imagen-model-options","text":"Gemini Imagen Model Options","level":4},{"id":"gemini-native-model-options-nanobanana","text":"Gemini Native Model Options (NanoBanana)","level":4},{"id":"response-format","text":"Response Format","level":3},{"id":"model-availability","text":"Model Availability","level":3},{"id":"openai-models-2","text":"OpenAI Models","level":4},{"id":"gemini-native-models-nanobanana-2","text":"Gemini Native Models (NanoBanana)","level":4},{"id":"gemini-imagen-models-2","text":"Gemini Imagen Models","level":4},{"id":"error-handling","text":"Error Handling","level":3},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment Variables","level":3},{"id":"explicit-api-keys","text":"Explicit API Keys","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack AI provides support for image generation through dedicated image adapters. This guide covers how to use the image generation functionality with OpenAI and Gemini providers.\n\n## Overview\n\nImage generation is handled by image adapters that follow the same tree-shakeable architecture as other adapters in TanStack AI. The image adapters support:\n\n- **OpenAI**: DALL-E 2, DALL-E 3, GPT-Image-1, GPT-Image-1-Mini, and GPT-Image-2 models\n- **Gemini**: Gemini native image models (NanoBanana) and Imagen 3/4 models\n- **BytePlus**: Seedream 5.0, 4.5, and 4.0 models\n- **fal.ai**: 600+ models including Nano Banana Pro, FLUX, and more\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n### OpenAI Image Generation\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\n// Generate an image (the adapter uses OPENAI_API_KEY from environment)\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"dall-e-3\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful sunset over mountains\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url); // URL to the generated image\n```\n\n### Gemini Image Generation\n\nGemini has two image model groups. Gemini native models (NanoBanana) use the Interactions API. Imagen models use `generateImages`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\n// Gemini native model (NanoBanana). Uses the Interactions API.\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at night\",\n  size: \"16:9_4K\",\n});\n\n// Imagen model. Uses the generateImages API.\nconst result2 = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"imagen-4.0-generate-001\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at night\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.b64Json); // Base64 encoded image\n```\n\n#### Edit a Gemini native image\n\nYou have an image from a Gemini native model. You want to change that image without a second upload of that image.\n\nPass the last `id` back. Write only the change in `prompt`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst adapter = geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\");\n\nconst first = await generateImage({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: \"A red bicycle on a quiet street\",\n});\n\nconst edited = await generateImage({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: \"Make the bicycle blue\",\n  modelOptions: { previous_interaction_id: first.id },\n});\n```\n\n1. Generate the first image.\n2. Call `generateImage` again with `previous_interaction_id` set to `first.id`.\n3. Read `edited.images` for the new picture.\n\nKeep the interaction so the next edit can run:\n\n1. Leave `store` unset.\n2. If you set `store` to `false`, a later call cannot use that id.\n\nThe API default for `store` is `true`.\n\nA free tier keeps a stored interaction for 1 day. A paid tier keeps it for 55 days.\n\nIf the model is Imagen, do not pass `previous_interaction_id`. The call throws.\n\nIf this edit needs a new reference image, add that image part on this call. Do not send the image from `first`.\n\nThe Interactions API is in Beta.\n\n`edited.images` holds the new picture. `edited.id` is the id for the next edit.\n\n### BytePlus Image Generation\n\nSeedream sizes take either a token (`1K`, `2K`, `4K`) or explicit pixels (`2048x2048`) — never a mix of the two.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { byteplusImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-byteplus\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: byteplusImage(\"dola-seedream-5-0-pro-260628\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at night\",\n  size: \"2K\",\n  modelOptions: { watermark: false },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url);\n```\n\nTwo Seedream behaviours differ from the other providers:\n\n- **`watermark` defaults to `true`** — BytePlus stamps \"AI generated\" into the corner unless you turn it off.\n- **`numberOfImages` is an upper bound, not a count.** Seedream has no `n` parameter, so more than one image maps onto its group-image mode and the model decides how many the prompt warrants. A request for four can return two.\n\nImage URLs expire after 24 hours; pass `response_format: 'b64_json'` in `modelOptions` for inline bytes. See the [BytePlus adapter](../adapters/byteplus#image-generation-seedream) for details.\n\n## Options\n\n### Common Options\n\nAll image adapters support these common options:\n\n| Option           | Type                          | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `adapter`        | `ImageAdapter`                | Image adapter instance with model (required)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| `prompt`         | `string \\| MediaPromptPart[]` | Description of the image to generate (required). A plain string, or — on models that support image-conditioned generation — an ordered array of content parts interleaving text with image inputs. See [Image-Conditioned Generation](#image-conditioned-generation) below. |\n| `numberOfImages` | `number`                      | Number of images to generate                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| `size`           | `string`                      | Size of the generated image in WIDTHxHEIGHT format                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| `modelOptions?`  | `object`                      | Model-specific options (renamed from `providerOptions`)                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n\n### Size Options\n\n#### OpenAI Models\n\n| Model                    | Supported Sizes                               |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `gpt-image-2.5-flare`    | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `gpt-image-2`            | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `gpt-image-1`            | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `gpt-image-1-mini`       | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `dall-e-3`               | `1024x1024`, `1792x1024`, `1024x1792`         |\n| `dall-e-2`               | `256x256`, `512x512`, `1024x1024`             |\n\n#### Gemini Native Models (NanoBanana)\n\nGemini native image models use a template literal size format: `\"aspectRatio_resolution\"`. Each model accepts its own set, narrowed at compile time:\n\n| Model                         | Aspect Ratios                                                                                          | Resolutions             |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------- |\n| `gemini-3.1-flash-image`      | `1:1`, `2:3`, `3:2`, `3:4`, `4:3`, `4:5`, `5:4`, `9:16`, `16:9`, `21:9`, `1:4`, `4:1`, `1:8`, `8:1` | `512`, `1K`, `2K`, `4K` |\n| `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` | same 14 as above (see note)                                                                             | `1K`                    |\n| `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`      | same 14 as above                                                                                        | `1K`, `2K`, `4K`        |\n| `gemini-3-pro-image`          | `1:1`, `2:3`, `3:2`, `3:4`, `4:3`, `4:5`, `5:4`, `9:16`, `16:9`, `21:9`                            | `1K`, `2K`, `4K`        |\n| `gemini-2.5-flash-image`      | same 10 as above                                                                                        | none — bare ratio       |\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Examples\nsize: \"16:9_4K\"; // Widescreen at 4K resolution\nsize: \"1:1_2K\"; // Square at 2K resolution\nsize: \"1:8_512\"; // Tall banner at the 512 (0.5K) tier — Flash Image only\nsize: \"16:9\"; // gemini-2.5-flash-image: bare ratio, no resolution suffix\n```\n\nThe `K` is case-sensitive (`1k` is rejected by the API), the smallest tier's token is `512` (not `512px` or `0.5K`), and `9:21` is Vertex/Cloud-only so it is not accepted. Google documents no `image_size` for `gemini-2.5-flash-image`, so that model takes a bare aspect ratio and the adapter sends no `imageSize`.\n\n> **Note on `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image`.** The four extreme banner ratios (`1:4`, `4:1`, `1:8`, `8:1`) are partially inferred for this model. Unlike the other three, Flash Lite has no per-model ratio table in Google's Gemini API guide; the 14-value set comes from the Cloud model page's explicit enumeration plus the guide's bare \"a discrete set of 14 aspect ratios\" assertion. The only Gemini-API enumeration for it is a 10-item bullet headed \"New aspect ratios\", which we read as a what's-new list rather than an exhaustive one. If the API rejects those four in practice, prefer the 10 standard ratios on this model.\n\n#### Gemini Imagen Models\n\nImagen models accept WIDTHxHEIGHT format, which maps to aspect ratios internally:\n\n| Size        | Aspect Ratio |\n| ----------- | ------------ |\n| `1024x1024` | 1:1          |\n| `1920x1080` | 16:9         |\n| `1080x1920` | 9:16         |\n\nAlternatively, you can specify the aspect ratio directly in Model Options:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"imagen-4.0-generate-001\"),\n  prompt: \"A landscape photo\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    aspectRatio: \"16:9\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Image-Conditioned Generation\n\nFor image-to-image, reference-guided, multi-reference, and edit / inpaint\nflows, pass the `prompt` as an ordered array of content parts — the same\n`TextPart` / `ImagePart` shapes used elsewhere for multimodal content:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Turn this into a cinematic product photo\" },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/product.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nPart order is meaningful. Providers with natively multimodal prompts\n(Gemini image models, OpenRouter) receive the parts exactly as written, so\ntext can refer to its neighbouring images:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\nimport { badExampleUrl, goodExampleUrl } from \"./urls\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Not like this\" },\n    { type: \"image\", source: { type: \"url\", value: badExampleUrl } },\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"more like this\" },\n    { type: \"image\", source: { type: \"url\", value: goodExampleUrl } },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nProviders with named request fields (OpenAI, fal, xAI) extract the image\nparts and flatten the text (text parts are joined verbatim, paragraph\nseparated).\n\nThe accepted part types are narrowed **per model at compile time**: passing\nan image part to a text-only model (e.g. `dall-e-3`, Imagen) is a type\nerror, not just a runtime throw.\n\n### Referencing images from your prompt\n\n**Your prompt text is always sent verbatim — the SDK never injects or\nrewrites referencing markers.** When you want the text to refer to specific\ninput images, write the provider's own convention yourself:\n\n| Provider                           | Convention                                              | Example                                                 |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **OpenAI** (gpt-image)             | Indexed prose, per OpenAI's prompting guide             | `\"apply the style of image 2 to image 1\"`               |\n| **FLUX.2 on fal / BFL**            | Indexed prose (BFL's docs parse `image N`)              | `\"subject from image 1, style from image 2\"`            |\n| **Gemini** (native image models)   | Describe the reference by content/role                  | `\"using the attached fabric sample as the texture\"`     |\n| **fal Kling / Seedance endpoints** | `@`-tags, 1-indexed by input order                      | `\"Put @Image1 in the style of @Image2\"`                 |\n| **xAI grok-imagine**               | No in-prompt syntax — images addressed in request order | `\"render the product in the style of the second image\"` |\n\nTo keep track of which part you meant by \"image 2\" or `@Image2`, you can\nlabel parts with the informational `metadata.tag` field — the SDK ignores\nit, but it keeps your code self-documenting:\n\n```typescript ignore\nprompt: [\n  { type: \"text\", content: \"Put @Image1 in the style of @Image2\" },\n  {\n    type: \"image\",\n    source: { type: \"url\", value: productUrl },\n    metadata: { tag: \"product\" },\n  },\n  {\n    type: \"image\",\n    source: { type: \"url\", value: styleUrl },\n    metadata: { tag: \"style\" },\n  },\n];\n```\n\n### Source format\n\n`ImagePart.source` is a discriminated union supporting both URLs and inline\nbase64 data — pass whichever you have:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// URL source\n{ type: 'image', source: { type: 'url', value: 'https://example.com/img.png' } }\n\n// Inline base64 data (mimeType required)\n{ type: 'image', source: { type: 'data', value: base64String, mimeType: 'image/png' } }\n```\n\nGemini native image generation does not download a URL in your runtime. The adapter sends the URL as `uri`. Gemini reads that URL. These sources work:\n\n- A public HTTPS URL\n- A [Files API](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/files) URI\n- A `gs://` reference\n\nTwo paths have no URL passthrough and must upload real bytes:\n\n- OpenAI's `/images/edits`, and Sora `input_reference`.\n- Gemini **Veo**: its predict API accepts only inline bytes or a `gs://`\n  reference.\n\nFor these, an HTTP(S) URL input would have to be downloaded and buffered in\nmemory, which can OOM memory-constrained runtimes (e.g. Cloudflare Workers). So\nby default they **throw** on an HTTP(S) URL image input rather than fetch it.\nPass a `data:` URI (or a `gs://` reference for Veo), or opt into fetching with\n`allowUrlFetch`:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createOpenaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\n// Opt into downloading + buffering HTTP(S) URL image inputs (server runtimes\n// with headroom). data: URIs always work without this flag.\nconst adapter = createOpenaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\", apiKey, {\n  allowUrlFetch: true,\n});\n```\n\nThe same `allowUrlFetch` option exists on `createOpenaiVideo` and\n`createGeminiVideo`.\n\n### Role hints via `metadata.role`\n\nWhen a generation has multiple inputs with different roles (mask vs reference\nvs start/end frame), set `metadata.role` on each part. Adapters route by role\nto the provider-specific field; parts without a role fall back to positional\nmapping.\n\n| Role            | Maps to                                                                          |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `'reference'`   | fal `reference_image_urls`; Gemini multimodal part; positional fallback          |\n| `'character'`   | Same as `'reference'`; Veo `referenceImages` slot (planned — no Veo adapter yet) |\n| `'mask'`        | OpenAI `mask` (gpt-image-2, gpt-image-1, dall-e-2); fal `mask_url`               |\n| `'control'`     | fal `control_image_url` (ControlNet / depth / pose conditioning)                 |\n| `'start_frame'` | fal `start_image_url`; Veo `image` (planned) (used by `generateVideo`)           |\n| `'end_frame'`   | fal `end_image_url`; Veo `lastFrame` (planned) (used by `generateVideo`)         |\n\n#### Inpaint / edit with a mask\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { photoUrl, maskUrl } from \"./urls\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Replace the masked region with a tree\" },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: photoUrl },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: maskUrl },\n      metadata: { role: \"mask\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n#### Multi-reference composition\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content:\n        \"Generate a new image of the product using the style of the second reference\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/product.png\" },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/style.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n### Provider support\n\n| Provider       | Behavior                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **OpenAI**     | `gpt-image-2.5-flare` / `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` / `gpt-image-2` / `gpt-image-1` / `gpt-image-1-mini` → routes to `images.edit()`, up to 16 source images plus optional mask.<br>`dall-e-2` → `images.edit()` with 1 source image only.<br>`dall-e-3` → throws (no edit support).                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| **Gemini**     | Native models send each prompt part as an Interactions content block, in the same order. Up to 14 input images. The SDK does not enforce that limit.<br>To edit the last image, pass `result.id` as `modelOptions.previous_interaction_id`. Do not send that image again. A new image part on that call is an extra reference. See [Edit a Gemini native image](#edit-a-gemini-native-image).<br>Imagen throws on an image part. Imagen does not chain. |\n| **fal.ai**     | Field names resolve per endpoint from a map generated from the fal SDK's endpoint types (e.g. nano-banana edit gets `image_urls`, Fooocus masks get `mask_image_url`). Defaults for unknown endpoints: 1 input → `image_url`; multiple → `image_urls`; `role: 'mask'` → `mask_url`; `role: 'control'` → `control_image_url`; `role: 'reference'` / `'character'` → `reference_image_urls`. Override with `modelOptions` for endpoint-specific fields. |\n| **Grok**       | grok-imagine models → xAI's `/v1/images/edits` (up to 3 source images, addressed by xAI in request order; prompt sent verbatim). `role: 'mask'` / `'control'` throw (no Imagine API equivalent).                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| **OpenRouter** | Prompt parts map 1:1 onto multimodal `image_url` / `text` content parts, preserving interleaved order, and are forwarded to the underlying image model. `modelOptions.strength` (0.0–1.0) controls image-to-image influence on models that document it (e.g. Recraft). One image per request — `numberOfImages > 1` throws (the gateway ignores count keys).                                                                                          |\n| **BytePlus**   | Seedream models → every input image is a plain reference on the `image` field (up to 14, or 10 on `dola-seedream-5-0-pro-260628`). There is no mask, control or frame channel, so any role other than `'reference'` / `'character'` throws rather than being silently flattened.                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| **Anthropic**  | n/a — no image generation API.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n\nAdapters that don't support image-conditioned generation throw a clear\nruntime error so calls fail fast rather than silently dropping the inputs.\n\n## Full-Stack Usage\n\nFor a React + Start walkthrough with OpenRouter, open [Generate Image](../tutorials/generate-image).\n\nTanStack AI provides React hooks and server-side streaming helpers to build full-stack image generation with minimal boilerplate.\n\n> **Note:** To keep a batch across reloads, or to keep the images after the\n> provider's URLs expire, add [Generation Persistence](../persistence/generation-persistence).\n\n### Streaming Mode (Server Route + Client Hook)\n\n**Server** — Create an API route that wraps `generateImage` as a streaming response:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/generate/image.ts\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { createFileRoute } from \"@tanstack/react-router\";\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute(\"/api/generate/image\")({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body = await request.json();\n        const { prompt, size, model, numberOfImages } = body.data;\n\n        const stream = generateImage({\n          adapter: openaiImage(model ?? \"dall-e-3\"),\n          prompt,\n          size,\n          numberOfImages,\n          stream: true,\n        });\n\n        return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n      },\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n**Client** — Use the `useGenerateImage` hook with a connection adapter:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, reset } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/generate/image\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: \"A sunset over mountains\" })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? \"Generating...\" : \"Generate\"}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img\n          key={i}\n          src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`}\n          alt={img.revisedPrompt || \"Generated image\"}\n        />\n      ))}\n      {result && <button onClick={reset}>Clear</button>}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe other two transports (a server function returning JSON, or one returning an\nSSE `Response`) work the same way here. They are in\n[Advanced: other transports](#other-transports), and explained once in\n[Generations](./generations#transports-in-full).\n\n### Hook API\n\nThe `useGenerateImage` hook accepts:\n\n| Option       | Type                                                    | Description                                                                                    |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `connection` | `ConnectionAdapter`                                     | Streaming transport (SSE, HTTP stream, custom)                                                 |\n| `fetcher`    | `(input) => Promise<ImageGenerationResult \\| Response>` | Direct async function, or server function returning an SSE `Response`                          |\n| `threadId`   | `string`                                                | Stable scope for this generation. Required when `persistence` is on. Optional for ephemeral runs. |\n| `body`       | `Record<string, any>`                                   | Additional body parameters (connection mode)                                                   |\n| `onResult`   | `(result) => TOutput \\| null \\| void`                   | Callback when images are generated. Optionally return a transformed value to store as `result` |\n| `onError`    | `(error) => void`                                       | Callback on error                                                                              |\n| `onProgress` | `(progress, message?) => void`                          | Progress updates (0-100)                                                                       |\n\nAnd returns:\n\n| Property    | Type                                           | Description                                            |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `generate`  | `(input: ImageGenerateInput) => Promise<void>` | Trigger generation                                     |\n| `result`    | `ImageGenerationResult \\| null`                | The result, or null                                    |\n| `isLoading` | `boolean`                                      | Whether generation is in progress                      |\n| `error`     | `Error \\| undefined`                           | Current error, if any                                  |\n| `status`    | `GenerationClientState`                        | `'idle'` \\| `'generating'` \\| `'success'` \\| `'error'` |\n| `stop`      | `() => void`                                   | Abort the current generation                           |\n| `reset`     | `() => void`                                   | Clear result, error, and return to idle                |\n\n> **Tip:** To trigger image generation from your React, Vue, or Svelte app with loading states and error handling, see [Generation Hooks](./generation-hooks).\n\n## Advanced\n\nReference detail you do not need to get this working.\n\n### Other transports\n\n#### Direct Mode (Server Function + Fetcher)\n\nFor non-streaming usage with TanStack Start server functions:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from \"@tanstack/react-start\";\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport const generateImageFn = createServerFn({ method: \"POST\" })\n  .inputValidator((data: { prompt: string; model?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    return generateImage({\n      adapter: openaiImage(data.model ?? \"dall-e-3\"),\n      prompt: data.prompt,\n    });\n  });\n```\n\n```tsx\n// components/ImageGenerator.tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { generateImageFn } from \"../lib/server-functions\";\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateImage({\n    fetcher: (data) => generateImageFn({ data }),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: \"A sunset over mountains\" })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img key={i} src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`} />\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n#### Server Function Streaming (Fetcher + Response)\n\nFor TanStack Start server functions that stream results. The fetcher receives type-safe input and returns an SSE `Response` — the client parses it automatically:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from \"@tanstack/react-start\";\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport const generateImageStreamFn = createServerFn({ method: \"POST\" })\n  .inputValidator((data: { prompt: string; model?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(({ data }) => {\n    return toServerSentEventsResponse(\n      generateImage({\n        adapter: openaiImage(data.model ?? \"dall-e-3\"),\n        prompt: data.prompt,\n        stream: true,\n      }),\n    );\n  });\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { generateImageStreamFn } from \"../lib/server-functions\";\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateImage({\n    fetcher: (input) => generateImageStreamFn({ data: input }),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: \"A sunset over mountains\" })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img key={i} src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`} />\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Model Options\n\n#### OpenAI Model Options\n\nOpenAI models support model-specific Model Options:\n\n##### GPT-Image-2 / GPT-Image-1 / GPT-Image-1-Mini\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"A cat wearing a hat\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    quality: \"high\", // 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' | 'auto'\n    background: \"transparent\", // 'transparent' | 'opaque' | 'auto'\n    output_format: \"png\", // 'png' | 'jpeg' | 'webp'\n    moderation: \"low\", // 'low' | 'auto'\n  },\n});\n```\n\n`gpt-image-2.5-flare` and `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` also take `quality: \"xhigh\"` and `quality: \"max\"`.\n\n##### DALL-E 3\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"dall-e-3\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic car\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    quality: \"hd\", // 'hd' | 'standard'\n    style: \"vivid\", // 'vivid' | 'natural'\n  },\n});\n```\n\n#### Gemini Imagen Model Options\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"imagen-4.0-generate-001\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful garden\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    aspectRatio: \"16:9\",\n    // personGeneration accepts PersonGeneration enum values: 'DONT_ALLOW' | 'ALLOW_ADULT' | 'ALLOW_ALL'\n    personGeneration: \"ALLOW_ADULT\",\n    negativePrompt: \"blurry, low quality\",\n    addWatermark: true,\n    outputMimeType: \"image/png\", // 'image/png' | 'image/jpeg' | 'image/webp'\n  },\n});\n```\n\n#### Gemini Native Model Options (NanoBanana)\n\nSet native image options on `modelOptions`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage, ThinkingLevel } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful garden\",\n  size: \"16:9_4K\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    seed: 42,\n    thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.LOW },\n    systemInstruction: \"Always render in watercolor.\",\n    // imageConfig replaces one field from size. The 16:9 ratio from size stays.\n    // imageConfig accepts only aspectRatio and imageSize.\n    imageConfig: { imageSize: \"2K\" },\n  },\n});\n```\n\nSet `thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel` to one of these values:\n\n- `ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL`\n- `ThinkingLevel.LOW`\n- `ThinkingLevel.MEDIUM`\n- `ThinkingLevel.HIGH`\n\n`thinkingConfig.thinkingBudget` throws.\n\nIf `systemInstruction` contains an image, a file, or a tool call, the call throws.\n\nPass the last result `id` as `previous_interaction_id`. Read [Edit a Gemini native image](#edit-a-gemini-native-image) for the edit steps.\n\n`safetySettings` takes the SDK's `HarmCategory` / `HarmBlockThreshold` enums, so plain strings won't type-check. Both are re-exported from `@tanstack/ai-gemini` — you don't need `@google/genai` in your own dependencies:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport {\n  HarmBlockThreshold,\n  HarmCategory,\n  geminiImage,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful garden\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    safetySettings: [\n      {\n        category: HarmCategory.HARM_CATEGORY_HATE_SPEECH,\n        threshold: HarmBlockThreshold.BLOCK_ONLY_HIGH,\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n});\n```\n\nThe adapter always requests an image.\n\n### Response Format\n\nThe image generation result includes:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { TokenUsage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\ninterface ImageGenerationResult {\n  id: string; // Unique identifier for this generation\n  model: string; // The model used\n  images: GeneratedImage[]; // Array of generated images\n  // Canonical TokenUsage (same shape as chat). Token-billed models also surface\n  // a per-modality breakdown on `promptTokensDetails` (e.g. text vs image input\n  // tokens for gpt-image-1). Usage-billed providers (fal) instead surface\n  // `usage.billed` ({ quantity, unit }) — see the note below.\n  usage?: TokenUsage;\n}\n\ninterface GeneratedImage {\n  b64Json?: string; // Base64 encoded image data\n  url?: string; // URL to the image (OpenAI only)\n  revisedPrompt?: string; // Revised prompt (OpenAI only)\n}\n```\n\nOn a Gemini native image model, `id` is the interaction id. Pass that id as `previous_interaction_id` on the next edit.\n\n> **Cost tracking (fal):** fal bills by usage-based units rather than tokens. The\n> fal image adapter surfaces the real billed quantity as `usage.billed` —\n> `{ quantity, unit: 'units' }`, read from fal's `x-fal-billable-units` result\n> header. Multiply the quantity by the endpoint's unit price from\n> `GET https://api.fal.ai/v1/models/pricing?endpoint_id=…` for the exact cost —\n> no `fetch` interceptor needed.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { falImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-fal\";\nimport { unitPrice } from \"./pricing\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: falImage(\"fal-ai/flux/dev\"),\n  prompt: \"a serene mountain lake\",\n});\n\nif (result.usage?.billed) {\n  const { quantity, unit } = result.usage.billed;\n  const cost = quantity * unitPrice; // unitPrice from fal pricing API\n  console.log(`Billed ${quantity} ${unit} (~$${cost})`);\n}\n```\n\n### Model Availability\n\n#### OpenAI Models\n\n| Model                    | Images per Request |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------ |\n| `gpt-image-2.5-flare`    | 1-10               |\n| `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` | 1-10               |\n| `gpt-image-2`            | 1-10               |\n| `gpt-image-1`            | 1-10               |\n| `gpt-image-1-mini`       | 1-10               |\n| `dall-e-3`               | 1                  |\n| `dall-e-2`               | 1-10               |\n\n#### Gemini Native Models (NanoBanana)\n\n| Model                         | Description                                                                |\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gemini-3.1-flash-image`      | Nano Banana 2 — latest and fastest Gemini native image generation          |\n| `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` | Nano Banana 2 Lite — ultra-low-latency, low-cost image generation          |\n| `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`      | Nano Banana 2.1 (1K/2K/4K, no 512 tier)                                    |\n| `gemini-3-pro-image`          | Nano Banana Pro — higher quality Gemini native image generation            |\n| `gemini-2.5-flash-image`      | Nano Banana — legacy; shuts down 2026-10-02                                |\n\nThe `gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview` and `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` ids were shut down on 2026-06-25. They remain in the type union as deprecated aliases so existing code compiles, but calls to them fail — use the GA ids above.\n\n#### Gemini Imagen Models\n\n| Model                           | Images per Request |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `imagen-4.0-ultra-generate-001` | 1-4                |\n| `imagen-4.0-generate-001`       | 1-4                |\n| `imagen-4.0-fast-generate-001`  | 1-4                |\n\n### Error Handling\n\nImage generation can fail for various reasons. The adapters validate inputs before making API calls:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\ntry {\n  const result = await generateImage({\n    adapter: openaiImage(\"dall-e-3\"),\n    prompt: \"A cat\",\n    size: \"512x512\", // Invalid size for DALL-E 3 — throws at runtime\n  });\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.error(error.message);\n    // \"Size \"512x512\" is not supported by model \"dall-e-3\".\n    //  Supported sizes: 1024x1024, 1792x1024, 1024x1792\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Environment Variables\n\nThe image adapters use the same environment variables as the text adapters:\n\n- **OpenAI**: `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n- **Gemini** (including NanoBanana): `GOOGLE_API_KEY` or `GEMINI_API_KEY`\n- **BytePlus** (Seedream): `ARK_API_KEY` or `BYTEPLUS_API_KEY`\n\n### Explicit API Keys\n\nFor production use or when you need explicit control:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { createGeminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\n// OpenAI\nconst openaiAdapter = createOpenaiImage(\"dall-e-3\", \"your-openai-api-key\");\n\n// Gemini\nconst geminiAdapter = createGeminiImage(\n  \"imagen-4.0-generate-001\",\n  \"your-google-api-key\",\n);\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Image Generation\nid: image-generation\norder: 5\ndescription: \"Generate images with OpenAI DALL-E, Gemini NanoBanana and Imagen, BytePlus Seedream, and fal.ai models via TanStack AI's unified generateImage() API.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - image generation\n  - generateImage\n  - dall-e\n  - imagen\n  - nano banana\n  - flux\n  - fal.ai\n---\n\nTanStack AI provides support for image generation through dedicated image adapters. This guide covers how to use the image generation functionality with OpenAI and Gemini providers.\n\n## Overview\n\nImage generation is handled by image adapters that follow the same tree-shakeable architecture as other adapters in TanStack AI. The image adapters support:\n\n- **OpenAI**: DALL-E 2, DALL-E 3, GPT-Image-1, GPT-Image-1-Mini, and GPT-Image-2 models\n- **Gemini**: Gemini native image models (NanoBanana) and Imagen 3/4 models\n- **BytePlus**: Seedream 5.0, 4.5, and 4.0 models\n- **fal.ai**: 600+ models including Nano Banana Pro, FLUX, and more\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n### OpenAI Image Generation\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\n// Generate an image (the adapter uses OPENAI_API_KEY from environment)\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"dall-e-3\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful sunset over mountains\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url); // URL to the generated image\n```\n\n### Gemini Image Generation\n\nGemini has two image model groups. Gemini native models (NanoBanana) use the Interactions API. Imagen models use `generateImages`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\n// Gemini native model (NanoBanana). Uses the Interactions API.\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at night\",\n  size: \"16:9_4K\",\n});\n\n// Imagen model. Uses the generateImages API.\nconst result2 = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"imagen-4.0-generate-001\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at night\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.b64Json); // Base64 encoded image\n```\n\n#### Edit a Gemini native image\n\nYou have an image from a Gemini native model. You want to change that image without a second upload of that image.\n\nPass the last `id` back. Write only the change in `prompt`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst adapter = geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\");\n\nconst first = await generateImage({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: \"A red bicycle on a quiet street\",\n});\n\nconst edited = await generateImage({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: \"Make the bicycle blue\",\n  modelOptions: { previous_interaction_id: first.id },\n});\n```\n\n1. Generate the first image.\n2. Call `generateImage` again with `previous_interaction_id` set to `first.id`.\n3. Read `edited.images` for the new picture.\n\nKeep the interaction so the next edit can run:\n\n1. Leave `store` unset.\n2. If you set `store` to `false`, a later call cannot use that id.\n\nThe API default for `store` is `true`.\n\nA free tier keeps a stored interaction for 1 day. A paid tier keeps it for 55 days.\n\nIf the model is Imagen, do not pass `previous_interaction_id`. The call throws.\n\nIf this edit needs a new reference image, add that image part on this call. Do not send the image from `first`.\n\nThe Interactions API is in Beta.\n\n`edited.images` holds the new picture. `edited.id` is the id for the next edit.\n\n### BytePlus Image Generation\n\nSeedream sizes take either a token (`1K`, `2K`, `4K`) or explicit pixels (`2048x2048`) — never a mix of the two.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { byteplusImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-byteplus\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: byteplusImage(\"dola-seedream-5-0-pro-260628\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at night\",\n  size: \"2K\",\n  modelOptions: { watermark: false },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url);\n```\n\nTwo Seedream behaviours differ from the other providers:\n\n- **`watermark` defaults to `true`** — BytePlus stamps \"AI generated\" into the corner unless you turn it off.\n- **`numberOfImages` is an upper bound, not a count.** Seedream has no `n` parameter, so more than one image maps onto its group-image mode and the model decides how many the prompt warrants. A request for four can return two.\n\nImage URLs expire after 24 hours; pass `response_format: 'b64_json'` in `modelOptions` for inline bytes. See the [BytePlus adapter](../adapters/byteplus#image-generation-seedream) for details.\n\n## Options\n\n### Common Options\n\nAll image adapters support these common options:\n\n| Option           | Type                          | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `adapter`        | `ImageAdapter`                | Image adapter instance with model (required)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| `prompt`         | `string \\| MediaPromptPart[]` | Description of the image to generate (required). A plain string, or — on models that support image-conditioned generation — an ordered array of content parts interleaving text with image inputs. See [Image-Conditioned Generation](#image-conditioned-generation) below. |\n| `numberOfImages` | `number`                      | Number of images to generate                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| `size`           | `string`                      | Size of the generated image in WIDTHxHEIGHT format                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| `modelOptions?`  | `object`                      | Model-specific options (renamed from `providerOptions`)                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n\n### Size Options\n\n#### OpenAI Models\n\n| Model                    | Supported Sizes                               |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `gpt-image-2.5-flare`    | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `gpt-image-2`            | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `gpt-image-1`            | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `gpt-image-1-mini`       | `1024x1024`, `1536x1024`, `1024x1536`, `auto` |\n| `dall-e-3`               | `1024x1024`, `1792x1024`, `1024x1792`         |\n| `dall-e-2`               | `256x256`, `512x512`, `1024x1024`             |\n\n#### Gemini Native Models (NanoBanana)\n\nGemini native image models use a template literal size format: `\"aspectRatio_resolution\"`. Each model accepts its own set, narrowed at compile time:\n\n| Model                         | Aspect Ratios                                                                                          | Resolutions             |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------- |\n| `gemini-3.1-flash-image`      | `1:1`, `2:3`, `3:2`, `3:4`, `4:3`, `4:5`, `5:4`, `9:16`, `16:9`, `21:9`, `1:4`, `4:1`, `1:8`, `8:1` | `512`, `1K`, `2K`, `4K` |\n| `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` | same 14 as above (see note)                                                                             | `1K`                    |\n| `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`      | same 14 as above                                                                                        | `1K`, `2K`, `4K`        |\n| `gemini-3-pro-image`          | `1:1`, `2:3`, `3:2`, `3:4`, `4:3`, `4:5`, `5:4`, `9:16`, `16:9`, `21:9`                            | `1K`, `2K`, `4K`        |\n| `gemini-2.5-flash-image`      | same 10 as above                                                                                        | none — bare ratio       |\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Examples\nsize: \"16:9_4K\"; // Widescreen at 4K resolution\nsize: \"1:1_2K\"; // Square at 2K resolution\nsize: \"1:8_512\"; // Tall banner at the 512 (0.5K) tier — Flash Image only\nsize: \"16:9\"; // gemini-2.5-flash-image: bare ratio, no resolution suffix\n```\n\nThe `K` is case-sensitive (`1k` is rejected by the API), the smallest tier's token is `512` (not `512px` or `0.5K`), and `9:21` is Vertex/Cloud-only so it is not accepted. Google documents no `image_size` for `gemini-2.5-flash-image`, so that model takes a bare aspect ratio and the adapter sends no `imageSize`.\n\n> **Note on `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image`.** The four extreme banner ratios (`1:4`, `4:1`, `1:8`, `8:1`) are partially inferred for this model. Unlike the other three, Flash Lite has no per-model ratio table in Google's Gemini API guide; the 14-value set comes from the Cloud model page's explicit enumeration plus the guide's bare \"a discrete set of 14 aspect ratios\" assertion. The only Gemini-API enumeration for it is a 10-item bullet headed \"New aspect ratios\", which we read as a what's-new list rather than an exhaustive one. If the API rejects those four in practice, prefer the 10 standard ratios on this model.\n\n#### Gemini Imagen Models\n\nImagen models accept WIDTHxHEIGHT format, which maps to aspect ratios internally:\n\n| Size        | Aspect Ratio |\n| ----------- | ------------ |\n| `1024x1024` | 1:1          |\n| `1920x1080` | 16:9         |\n| `1080x1920` | 9:16         |\n\nAlternatively, you can specify the aspect ratio directly in Model Options:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"imagen-4.0-generate-001\"),\n  prompt: \"A landscape photo\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    aspectRatio: \"16:9\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Image-Conditioned Generation\n\nFor image-to-image, reference-guided, multi-reference, and edit / inpaint\nflows, pass the `prompt` as an ordered array of content parts — the same\n`TextPart` / `ImagePart` shapes used elsewhere for multimodal content:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Turn this into a cinematic product photo\" },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/product.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nPart order is meaningful. Providers with natively multimodal prompts\n(Gemini image models, OpenRouter) receive the parts exactly as written, so\ntext can refer to its neighbouring images:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\nimport { badExampleUrl, goodExampleUrl } from \"./urls\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Not like this\" },\n    { type: \"image\", source: { type: \"url\", value: badExampleUrl } },\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"more like this\" },\n    { type: \"image\", source: { type: \"url\", value: goodExampleUrl } },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nProviders with named request fields (OpenAI, fal, xAI) extract the image\nparts and flatten the text (text parts are joined verbatim, paragraph\nseparated).\n\nThe accepted part types are narrowed **per model at compile time**: passing\nan image part to a text-only model (e.g. `dall-e-3`, Imagen) is a type\nerror, not just a runtime throw.\n\n### Referencing images from your prompt\n\n**Your prompt text is always sent verbatim — the SDK never injects or\nrewrites referencing markers.** When you want the text to refer to specific\ninput images, write the provider's own convention yourself:\n\n| Provider                           | Convention                                              | Example                                                 |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **OpenAI** (gpt-image)             | Indexed prose, per OpenAI's prompting guide             | `\"apply the style of image 2 to image 1\"`               |\n| **FLUX.2 on fal / BFL**            | Indexed prose (BFL's docs parse `image N`)              | `\"subject from image 1, style from image 2\"`            |\n| **Gemini** (native image models)   | Describe the reference by content/role                  | `\"using the attached fabric sample as the texture\"`     |\n| **fal Kling / Seedance endpoints** | `@`-tags, 1-indexed by input order                      | `\"Put @Image1 in the style of @Image2\"`                 |\n| **xAI grok-imagine**               | No in-prompt syntax — images addressed in request order | `\"render the product in the style of the second image\"` |\n\nTo keep track of which part you meant by \"image 2\" or `@Image2`, you can\nlabel parts with the informational `metadata.tag` field — the SDK ignores\nit, but it keeps your code self-documenting:\n\n```typescript ignore\nprompt: [\n  { type: \"text\", content: \"Put @Image1 in the style of @Image2\" },\n  {\n    type: \"image\",\n    source: { type: \"url\", value: productUrl },\n    metadata: { tag: \"product\" },\n  },\n  {\n    type: \"image\",\n    source: { type: \"url\", value: styleUrl },\n    metadata: { tag: \"style\" },\n  },\n];\n```\n\n### Source format\n\n`ImagePart.source` is a discriminated union supporting both URLs and inline\nbase64 data — pass whichever you have:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// URL source\n{ type: 'image', source: { type: 'url', value: 'https://example.com/img.png' } }\n\n// Inline base64 data (mimeType required)\n{ type: 'image', source: { type: 'data', value: base64String, mimeType: 'image/png' } }\n```\n\nGemini native image generation does not download a URL in your runtime. The adapter sends the URL as `uri`. Gemini reads that URL. These sources work:\n\n- A public HTTPS URL\n- A [Files API](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/files) URI\n- A `gs://` reference\n\nTwo paths have no URL passthrough and must upload real bytes:\n\n- OpenAI's `/images/edits`, and Sora `input_reference`.\n- Gemini **Veo**: its predict API accepts only inline bytes or a `gs://`\n  reference.\n\nFor these, an HTTP(S) URL input would have to be downloaded and buffered in\nmemory, which can OOM memory-constrained runtimes (e.g. Cloudflare Workers). So\nby default they **throw** on an HTTP(S) URL image input rather than fetch it.\nPass a `data:` URI (or a `gs://` reference for Veo), or opt into fetching with\n`allowUrlFetch`:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createOpenaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\n// Opt into downloading + buffering HTTP(S) URL image inputs (server runtimes\n// with headroom). data: URIs always work without this flag.\nconst adapter = createOpenaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\", apiKey, {\n  allowUrlFetch: true,\n});\n```\n\nThe same `allowUrlFetch` option exists on `createOpenaiVideo` and\n`createGeminiVideo`.\n\n### Role hints via `metadata.role`\n\nWhen a generation has multiple inputs with different roles (mask vs reference\nvs start/end frame), set `metadata.role` on each part. Adapters route by role\nto the provider-specific field; parts without a role fall back to positional\nmapping.\n\n| Role            | Maps to                                                                          |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `'reference'`   | fal `reference_image_urls`; Gemini multimodal part; positional fallback          |\n| `'character'`   | Same as `'reference'`; Veo `referenceImages` slot (planned — no Veo adapter yet) |\n| `'mask'`        | OpenAI `mask` (gpt-image-2, gpt-image-1, dall-e-2); fal `mask_url`               |\n| `'control'`     | fal `control_image_url` (ControlNet / depth / pose conditioning)                 |\n| `'start_frame'` | fal `start_image_url`; Veo `image` (planned) (used by `generateVideo`)           |\n| `'end_frame'`   | fal `end_image_url`; Veo `lastFrame` (planned) (used by `generateVideo`)         |\n\n#### Inpaint / edit with a mask\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { photoUrl, maskUrl } from \"./urls\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Replace the masked region with a tree\" },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: photoUrl },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: maskUrl },\n      metadata: { role: \"mask\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n#### Multi-reference composition\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nawait generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content:\n        \"Generate a new image of the product using the style of the second reference\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/product.png\" },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/style.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n### Provider support\n\n| Provider       | Behavior                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **OpenAI**     | `gpt-image-2.5-flare` / `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` / `gpt-image-2` / `gpt-image-1` / `gpt-image-1-mini` → routes to `images.edit()`, up to 16 source images plus optional mask.<br>`dall-e-2` → `images.edit()` with 1 source image only.<br>`dall-e-3` → throws (no edit support).                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| **Gemini**     | Native models send each prompt part as an Interactions content block, in the same order. Up to 14 input images. The SDK does not enforce that limit.<br>To edit the last image, pass `result.id` as `modelOptions.previous_interaction_id`. Do not send that image again. A new image part on that call is an extra reference. See [Edit a Gemini native image](#edit-a-gemini-native-image).<br>Imagen throws on an image part. Imagen does not chain. |\n| **fal.ai**     | Field names resolve per endpoint from a map generated from the fal SDK's endpoint types (e.g. nano-banana edit gets `image_urls`, Fooocus masks get `mask_image_url`). Defaults for unknown endpoints: 1 input → `image_url`; multiple → `image_urls`; `role: 'mask'` → `mask_url`; `role: 'control'` → `control_image_url`; `role: 'reference'` / `'character'` → `reference_image_urls`. Override with `modelOptions` for endpoint-specific fields. |\n| **Grok**       | grok-imagine models → xAI's `/v1/images/edits` (up to 3 source images, addressed by xAI in request order; prompt sent verbatim). `role: 'mask'` / `'control'` throw (no Imagine API equivalent).                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| **OpenRouter** | Prompt parts map 1:1 onto multimodal `image_url` / `text` content parts, preserving interleaved order, and are forwarded to the underlying image model. `modelOptions.strength` (0.0–1.0) controls image-to-image influence on models that document it (e.g. Recraft). One image per request — `numberOfImages > 1` throws (the gateway ignores count keys).                                                                                          |\n| **BytePlus**   | Seedream models → every input image is a plain reference on the `image` field (up to 14, or 10 on `dola-seedream-5-0-pro-260628`). There is no mask, control or frame channel, so any role other than `'reference'` / `'character'` throws rather than being silently flattened.                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| **Anthropic**  | n/a — no image generation API.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n\nAdapters that don't support image-conditioned generation throw a clear\nruntime error so calls fail fast rather than silently dropping the inputs.\n\n## Full-Stack Usage\n\nFor a React + Start walkthrough with OpenRouter, open [Generate Image](../tutorials/generate-image).\n\nTanStack AI provides React hooks and server-side streaming helpers to build full-stack image generation with minimal boilerplate.\n\n> **Note:** To keep a batch across reloads, or to keep the images after the\n> provider's URLs expire, add [Generation Persistence](../persistence/generation-persistence).\n\n### Streaming Mode (Server Route + Client Hook)\n\n**Server** — Create an API route that wraps `generateImage` as a streaming response:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/generate/image.ts\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { createFileRoute } from \"@tanstack/react-router\";\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute(\"/api/generate/image\")({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body = await request.json();\n        const { prompt, size, model, numberOfImages } = body.data;\n\n        const stream = generateImage({\n          adapter: openaiImage(model ?? \"dall-e-3\"),\n          prompt,\n          size,\n          numberOfImages,\n          stream: true,\n        });\n\n        return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n      },\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n**Client** — Use the `useGenerateImage` hook with a connection adapter:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, reset } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/generate/image\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: \"A sunset over mountains\" })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? \"Generating...\" : \"Generate\"}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img\n          key={i}\n          src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`}\n          alt={img.revisedPrompt || \"Generated image\"}\n        />\n      ))}\n      {result && <button onClick={reset}>Clear</button>}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe other two transports (a server function returning JSON, or one returning an\nSSE `Response`) work the same way here. They are in\n[Advanced: other transports](#other-transports), and explained once in\n[Generations](./generations#transports-in-full).\n\n### Hook API\n\nThe `useGenerateImage` hook accepts:\n\n| Option       | Type                                                    | Description                                                                                    |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `connection` | `ConnectionAdapter`                                     | Streaming transport (SSE, HTTP stream, custom)                                                 |\n| `fetcher`    | `(input) => Promise<ImageGenerationResult \\| Response>` | Direct async function, or server function returning an SSE `Response`                          |\n| `threadId`   | `string`                                                | Stable scope for this generation. Required when `persistence` is on. Optional for ephemeral runs. |\n| `body`       | `Record<string, any>`                                   | Additional body parameters (connection mode)                                                   |\n| `onResult`   | `(result) => TOutput \\| null \\| void`                   | Callback when images are generated. Optionally return a transformed value to store as `result` |\n| `onError`    | `(error) => void`                                       | Callback on error                                                                              |\n| `onProgress` | `(progress, message?) => void`                          | Progress updates (0-100)                                                                       |\n\nAnd returns:\n\n| Property    | Type                                           | Description                                            |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `generate`  | `(input: ImageGenerateInput) => Promise<void>` | Trigger generation                                     |\n| `result`    | `ImageGenerationResult \\| null`                | The result, or null                                    |\n| `isLoading` | `boolean`                                      | Whether generation is in progress                      |\n| `error`     | `Error \\| undefined`                           | Current error, if any                                  |\n| `status`    | `GenerationClientState`                        | `'idle'` \\| `'generating'` \\| `'success'` \\| `'error'` |\n| `stop`      | `() => void`                                   | Abort the current generation                           |\n| `reset`     | `() => void`                                   | Clear result, error, and return to idle                |\n\n> **Tip:** To trigger image generation from your React, Vue, or Svelte app with loading states and error handling, see [Generation Hooks](./generation-hooks).\n\n## Advanced\n\nReference detail you do not need to get this working.\n\n### Other transports\n\n#### Direct Mode (Server Function + Fetcher)\n\nFor non-streaming usage with TanStack Start server functions:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from \"@tanstack/react-start\";\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport const generateImageFn = createServerFn({ method: \"POST\" })\n  .inputValidator((data: { prompt: string; model?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    return generateImage({\n      adapter: openaiImage(data.model ?? \"dall-e-3\"),\n      prompt: data.prompt,\n    });\n  });\n```\n\n```tsx\n// components/ImageGenerator.tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { generateImageFn } from \"../lib/server-functions\";\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateImage({\n    fetcher: (data) => generateImageFn({ data }),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: \"A sunset over mountains\" })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img key={i} src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`} />\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n#### Server Function Streaming (Fetcher + Response)\n\nFor TanStack Start server functions that stream results. The fetcher receives type-safe input and returns an SSE `Response` — the client parses it automatically:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from \"@tanstack/react-start\";\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport const generateImageStreamFn = createServerFn({ method: \"POST\" })\n  .inputValidator((data: { prompt: string; model?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(({ data }) => {\n    return toServerSentEventsResponse(\n      generateImage({\n        adapter: openaiImage(data.model ?? \"dall-e-3\"),\n        prompt: data.prompt,\n        stream: true,\n      }),\n    );\n  });\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { generateImageStreamFn } from \"../lib/server-functions\";\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateImage({\n    fetcher: (input) => generateImageStreamFn({ data: input }),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: \"A sunset over mountains\" })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img key={i} src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`} />\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Model Options\n\n#### OpenAI Model Options\n\nOpenAI models support model-specific Model Options:\n\n##### GPT-Image-2 / GPT-Image-1 / GPT-Image-1-Mini\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"A cat wearing a hat\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    quality: \"high\", // 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' | 'auto'\n    background: \"transparent\", // 'transparent' | 'opaque' | 'auto'\n    output_format: \"png\", // 'png' | 'jpeg' | 'webp'\n    moderation: \"low\", // 'low' | 'auto'\n  },\n});\n```\n\n`gpt-image-2.5-flare` and `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` also take `quality: \"xhigh\"` and `quality: \"max\"`.\n\n##### DALL-E 3\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"dall-e-3\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic car\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    quality: \"hd\", // 'hd' | 'standard'\n    style: \"vivid\", // 'vivid' | 'natural'\n  },\n});\n```\n\n#### Gemini Imagen Model Options\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"imagen-4.0-generate-001\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful garden\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    aspectRatio: \"16:9\",\n    // personGeneration accepts PersonGeneration enum values: 'DONT_ALLOW' | 'ALLOW_ADULT' | 'ALLOW_ALL'\n    personGeneration: \"ALLOW_ADULT\",\n    negativePrompt: \"blurry, low quality\",\n    addWatermark: true,\n    outputMimeType: \"image/png\", // 'image/png' | 'image/jpeg' | 'image/webp'\n  },\n});\n```\n\n#### Gemini Native Model Options (NanoBanana)\n\nSet native image options on `modelOptions`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { geminiImage, ThinkingLevel } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful garden\",\n  size: \"16:9_4K\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    seed: 42,\n    thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.LOW },\n    systemInstruction: \"Always render in watercolor.\",\n    // imageConfig replaces one field from size. The 16:9 ratio from size stays.\n    // imageConfig accepts only aspectRatio and imageSize.\n    imageConfig: { imageSize: \"2K\" },\n  },\n});\n```\n\nSet `thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel` to one of these values:\n\n- `ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL`\n- `ThinkingLevel.LOW`\n- `ThinkingLevel.MEDIUM`\n- `ThinkingLevel.HIGH`\n\n`thinkingConfig.thinkingBudget` throws.\n\nIf `systemInstruction` contains an image, a file, or a tool call, the call throws.\n\nPass the last result `id` as `previous_interaction_id`. Read [Edit a Gemini native image](#edit-a-gemini-native-image) for the edit steps.\n\n`safetySettings` takes the SDK's `HarmCategory` / `HarmBlockThreshold` enums, so plain strings won't type-check. Both are re-exported from `@tanstack/ai-gemini` — you don't need `@google/genai` in your own dependencies:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport {\n  HarmBlockThreshold,\n  HarmCategory,\n  geminiImage,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: geminiImage(\"gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A beautiful garden\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    safetySettings: [\n      {\n        category: HarmCategory.HARM_CATEGORY_HATE_SPEECH,\n        threshold: HarmBlockThreshold.BLOCK_ONLY_HIGH,\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n});\n```\n\nThe adapter always requests an image.\n\n### Response Format\n\nThe image generation result includes:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { TokenUsage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\ninterface ImageGenerationResult {\n  id: string; // Unique identifier for this generation\n  model: string; // The model used\n  images: GeneratedImage[]; // Array of generated images\n  // Canonical TokenUsage (same shape as chat). Token-billed models also surface\n  // a per-modality breakdown on `promptTokensDetails` (e.g. text vs image input\n  // tokens for gpt-image-1). Usage-billed providers (fal) instead surface\n  // `usage.billed` ({ quantity, unit }) — see the note below.\n  usage?: TokenUsage;\n}\n\ninterface GeneratedImage {\n  b64Json?: string; // Base64 encoded image data\n  url?: string; // URL to the image (OpenAI only)\n  revisedPrompt?: string; // Revised prompt (OpenAI only)\n}\n```\n\nOn a Gemini native image model, `id` is the interaction id. Pass that id as `previous_interaction_id` on the next edit.\n\n> **Cost tracking (fal):** fal bills by usage-based units rather than tokens. The\n> fal image adapter surfaces the real billed quantity as `usage.billed` —\n> `{ quantity, unit: 'units' }`, read from fal's `x-fal-billable-units` result\n> header. Multiply the quantity by the endpoint's unit price from\n> `GET https://api.fal.ai/v1/models/pricing?endpoint_id=…` for the exact cost —\n> no `fetch` interceptor needed.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { falImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-fal\";\nimport { unitPrice } from \"./pricing\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: falImage(\"fal-ai/flux/dev\"),\n  prompt: \"a serene mountain lake\",\n});\n\nif (result.usage?.billed) {\n  const { quantity, unit } = result.usage.billed;\n  const cost = quantity * unitPrice; // unitPrice from fal pricing API\n  console.log(`Billed ${quantity} ${unit} (~$${cost})`);\n}\n```\n\n### Model Availability\n\n#### OpenAI Models\n\n| Model                    | Images per Request |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------ |\n| `gpt-image-2.5-flare`    | 1-10               |\n| `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` | 1-10               |\n| `gpt-image-2`            | 1-10               |\n| `gpt-image-1`            | 1-10               |\n| `gpt-image-1-mini`       | 1-10               |\n| `dall-e-3`               | 1                  |\n| `dall-e-2`               | 1-10               |\n\n#### Gemini Native Models (NanoBanana)\n\n| Model                         | Description                                                                |\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gemini-3.1-flash-image`      | Nano Banana 2 — latest and fastest Gemini native image generation          |\n| `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` | Nano Banana 2 Lite — ultra-low-latency, low-cost image generation          |\n| `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`      | Nano Banana 2.1 (1K/2K/4K, no 512 tier)                                    |\n| `gemini-3-pro-image`          | Nano Banana Pro — higher quality Gemini native image generation            |\n| `gemini-2.5-flash-image`      | Nano Banana — legacy; shuts down 2026-10-02                                |\n\nThe `gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview` and `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` ids were shut down on 2026-06-25. They remain in the type union as deprecated aliases so existing code compiles, but calls to them fail — use the GA ids above.\n\n#### Gemini Imagen Models\n\n| Model                           | Images per Request |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `imagen-4.0-ultra-generate-001` | 1-4                |\n| `imagen-4.0-generate-001`       | 1-4                |\n| `imagen-4.0-fast-generate-001`  | 1-4                |\n\n### Error Handling\n\nImage generation can fail for various reasons. The adapters validate inputs before making API calls:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\ntry {\n  const result = await generateImage({\n    adapter: openaiImage(\"dall-e-3\"),\n    prompt: \"A cat\",\n    size: \"512x512\", // Invalid size for DALL-E 3 — throws at runtime\n  });\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.error(error.message);\n    // \"Size \"512x512\" is not supported by model \"dall-e-3\".\n    //  Supported sizes: 1024x1024, 1792x1024, 1024x1792\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Environment Variables\n\nThe image adapters use the same environment variables as the text adapters:\n\n- **OpenAI**: `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n- **Gemini** (including NanoBanana): `GOOGLE_API_KEY` or `GEMINI_API_KEY`\n- **BytePlus** (Seedream): `ARK_API_KEY` or `BYTEPLUS_API_KEY`\n\n### Explicit API Keys\n\nFor production use or when you need explicit control:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { createGeminiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-gemini\";\n\n// OpenAI\nconst openaiAdapter = createOpenaiImage(\"dall-e-3\", \"your-openai-api-key\");\n\n// Gemini\nconst geminiAdapter = createGeminiImage(\n  \"imagen-4.0-generate-001\",\n  \"your-google-api-key\",\n);\n```\n"}
